menu "Dancefloor hub"

    config DANCEFLOOR_NOMINAL_RATE
        int "Nominal audio sample rate (Hz)"
        default 44100
        help
            Seeds the presentation timeline until the first SBC frame reports
            the real rate, so it only needs to be roughly right.

    comment "I2S output -- to this unit's own DAC (this chip is the MASTER)"

    config DANCEFLOOR_I2S_LRCK_PIN
        int "I2S LRCK (WS) GPIO"
        default 27

    config DANCEFLOOR_I2S_BCK_PIN
        int "I2S BCK GPIO"
        default 26

    config DANCEFLOOR_I2S_DATA_PIN
        int "I2S DATA GPIO"
        default 25

    config DANCEFLOOR_WIFI_CHANNEL
        int "SoftAP channel (1-13)"
        default 11
        help
            Pinned rather than driver-chosen: Bluetooth's adaptive frequency
            hopping avoids a WiFi interferer far more effectively when it sits on
            a fixed, known slice of the band. Costs nothing.

    config DANCEFLOOR_WIFI_PHY_RATE_MBPS
        int "Fixed multicast PHY rate in Mbps (6, 12, 24; 0 = driver default)"
        default 6
        help
            Multicast must be pinned, and the rate is a real tradeoff measured on
            this hardware:

              driver default -> falls back to the 1 Mbps basic rate. A 1041-byte
                                frame takes 8.3 ms, and 172 packets/s needs 1.43
                                seconds of airtime per second. 52% loss.
              24 Mbps        -> only 6% airtime, but needs good SNR and
                                multicast is never retried. 23% loss.
              6 Mbps         -> 24% airtime, far more robust. The compromise.

            Forwarding SBC rather than PCM would cut all of these by four.

    config DANCEFLOOR_AP_OPEN
        bool "Run the SoftAP with no password (diagnostic)"
        default n
        help
            Isolates the WPA2 handshake. If clients associate with this on but
            not off, the problem is the security config; if they fail either way,
            the AP itself is not coming up properly and the credentials are a red
            herring. Satellites must be built to match.

    comment "Diagnostics"

    config DANCEFLOOR_VERIFY_PATTERN
        bool "Verify counter test pattern on the I2S input"
        default n
        help
            Expects the bridge to be running i2s_loopback in TX_ONLY mode rather
            than real audio. Counts actually-missing samples instead of inferring
            loss from a rate deficit -- and unlike the standalone loopback test,
            it does so with WiFi, streaming and playback all running.

    config DANCEFLOOR_NO_STREAM_TX
        bool "Bring WiFi up but do not multicast audio"
        default n
        help
            Separates the radio simply being associated and beaconing from the
            load of pushing ~170 audio packets/s. Local playback continues.

    comment "LEDs"

    config DANCEFLOOR_ENABLE_VISUALISER
        bool "Enable LED visualiser (FFT + strip)"
        default y
        help
            Turn off to test whether the FFT and LED refresh are stealing time
            from the I2S receive task. With a clean I2S link the loopback test
            loses zero frames on an idle chip; the hub loses ~1.3%, and the
            visualiser is the heaviest thing sharing its core.


    config DANCEFLOOR_LED_GPIO
        int "WS2812 data GPIO"
        default 18
        help
            SPI2 MOSI via the GPIO matrix. Needs a 74AHCT125 level shifter:
            3.3 V data into a 5 V WS2812 is unreliable without one.

    config DANCEFLOOR_LED_COUNT
        int "Number of LEDs"
        default 60

endmenu
